<article class="env-corollary" id="00ZF">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00ZF">Corollary <span data-tag="00ZF">3.3.6.5</span>.</a> Let $f: X \rightarrow S$ be a morphism of simplicial sets. Let $s$ be a vertex of $S$, which we will identify (via Proposition <a data-tag="00ZC" href="/tag/00ZC">3.3.6.2</a>) with its image in $\operatorname{Ex}^{\infty }(S)$. Then the canonical map $\operatorname{Ex}^{\infty }( X_ s ) \rightarrow \operatorname{Ex}^{\infty }(X)_{s}$ is an isomorphism of simplicial sets. Here $X_ s = \{ s\}  \times _{S} X$ denotes the fiber of $f$ over the vertex $s$, and $\operatorname{Ex}^{\infty }(X)_{s} = \{ s\}  \times _{ \operatorname{Ex}^{\infty }(S) } \operatorname{Ex}^{\infty }(X)$ is defined similarly. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Proposition <a data-tag="00ZE" href="/tag/00ZE">3.3.6.4</a> with Example <a data-tag="00ZD" href="/tag/00ZD">3.3.6.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
